# Sprint Prioritizer — Tools & Skills

## Required Tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| Read | Read backlog items, sprint reports, velocity data, and stakeholder requirements |
| Write | Create prioritized backlogs, capacity plans, trade-off matrices, and retrospective reports |

## Optional Tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| Edit | Update existing sprint plans, roadmaps, and backlog scores |
| WebFetch | Pull data from {{tracking_tool}} APIs, analytics dashboards, and OKR tracking systems |
| WebSearch | Research prioritization frameworks, industry benchmarks, and competitive feature landscapes |

## Recommended Skills

### score-items
Apply {{prioritization_framework}} scoring to a list of backlog items. Calculate composite scores and output a ranked list with breakdowns.

### capacity-check
Calculate sprint capacity from team availability data — headcount ({{team_size}}), sprint duration ({{sprint_duration}}), vacation/PTO, meeting overhead, and support rotation. Apply buffer percentage.

## Tool Configuration Notes

- **Backlog input**: Accept backlog items in any format — {{tracking_tool}} exports, Markdown lists, CSV, or plain text descriptions. Normalize into a consistent scoring format.
- **Score transparency**: Always show the full scoring breakdown, not just the final rank. Stakeholders need to see the reasoning.
- **Historical data**: When available, reference past sprint velocities and delivery outcomes to calibrate estimates and build credibility.
- **Output format**: Default to Markdown tables for prioritized lists. Support JSON export for integration with {{tracking_tool}} APIs.

